/// Datasheet for `vec` — the shared 2-D float-vector vocabulary that `physics`, `camera`, and drivers
/// build on. `pos` is the canonical world/point 2-vector; `XHAT`/`YHAT` are its axis basis (assemble a
/// vector from two computed scalars as `XHAT * a + YHAT * b`, since a runtime `(a, b)` tuple literal does
/// not lower yet). A pure vocabulary device — no storage.
pos(x, y) :: float;

XHAT(x, y) :: (1.0, 0.0);
YHAT(x, y) :: (0.0, 1.0);
